Post 12: AI/ML Ops Engineer Interview
Senior Level (5–8 Years)

Scaling machine learning in production — where models meet reliability, automation, and traceability! 🤖 

At this level, you’re engineering MLOps platforms, automating model lifecycles, and ensuring experiment-to-production pipelines are auditable, secure, and fast.

Test your applied AI Infrastructure & MLOps mastery 👇

💡 Common AI/ML Ops Interview Questions (5–8 Years Experience): 
1️⃣ How do you design a feature store for cross-team collaboration and reuse? 
2️⃣ Explain your CI/CD for ML models — from data ingestion to model deployment. 
3️⃣ What’s your approach to model versioning and lineage tracking (e.g., MLflow, Vertex AI, DVC)? 
4️⃣ How do you orchestrate training and inference pipelines using Kubeflow, Airflow, or Vertex Pipelines? 
5️⃣ What’s your monitoring strategy for drift detection and model performance in production? 
6️⃣ Explain data governance and security controls for sensitive ML datasets. 
7️⃣ How do you implement infrastructure scaling for distributed training (GPUs, TPUs, spot instances)? 
8️⃣ Describe your use of automated testing in the ML lifecycle (unit, data, model validation). 
9️⃣ How do you optimize cost and performance trade-offs in training and inference environments? 
🔟 What’s your strategy for cross-functional collaboration between data scientists, ML engineers, and DevOps teams?
🎯 Pro Tip: 
Senior MLOps engineers treat data as code & models as artifacts — “Our pipeline reduced model retraining from 48 hours to 4 hours while improving AUC by 6%.” 
Balance innovation and reproducibility — fast ML must still be trustworthy ML.

